meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    producer: Centers for Disease Control and Prevention
    title: National Notifiable Diseases Surveillance System (NNDSS) Weekly Data
    description: |-
      Provisional weekly counts of reported measles cases in the United States, by reporting area (US regions, states, New York City and US territories), split into indigenous cases (infected in the United States) and imported cases (infected outside the United States). For each week, the data gives the cases reported that week and the cumulative count for the year so far. New York State figures exclude New York City, which reports separately.

      These counts are provisional and can change as states finish their case investigations. The CDC later publishes finalized annual counts, which can differ from the provisional ones.
    date_published: "2026-11-04"
    # Citation
    citation_full: |-
      Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. National Notifiable Diseases Surveillance System (NNDSS) Weekly Data. Office of Public Health Data, Surveillance, and Technology, Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, 2026.
    attribution_short: CDC
